Revision: commit "M4.4: lease-fenced run plane — a second core on the
store fences the first mid-run" on main
Environment: macOS darwin 25.5.0 arm64, local dev profile, UTC

WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: SCAFFOLDED-in-production — the store's
lease-fenced append (append_with_lease, typed StaleLease, unit-proven in
lease_resume.rs since M1) had ZERO production callers; the scheduler's
run plane wrote unfenced)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- run_task_inner acquires the session lease at run start
  (leases::acquire bumps the generation — any writer that starts later
  for the same session immediately stales this one).
- EventStoreObserver appends and the Phase 2.6 output sink's chunk
  appends route through RunPlaneShared::append_fenced.
- A StaleLease rejection flips the fence flag AND the run's cancellation
  token: the provider stream aborts (transport select), the broker run
  is killed (no orphan process), and the turn boundary aborts — the
  fenced writer writes NOTHING further and never continues; its run
  dangles while the takeover writer owns the session.
- The command plane (surface CommandProcessor) stays unfenced by design:
  multi-client command intake is a separate concern from the single
  mutation owner of the run plane.

